<refentry id="timestampd.conf" conditional='ENABLE_TIMESTAMPD'
    xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <refentryinfo>
    <title>timestampd.conf</title>
    <productname>systemd</productname>
  </refentryinfo>

  <refmeta>
    <refentrytitle>timestampd.conf</refentrytitle>
    <manvolnum>5</manvolnum>
  </refmeta>

  <refnamediv>
    <refname>timestampd.conf</refname>
    <refname>timestampd.conf.d</refname>
    <refpurpose>Time-stamp acquisition service configuration files</refpurpose>
  </refnamediv>

  <refsynopsisdiv>
    <para><simplelist>
      <member><filename>/etc/systemd/timestampd.conf</filename></member>
      <member><filename>/run/systemd/timestampd.conf</filename></member>
      <member><filename>/usr/local/lib/systemd/timestampd.conf</filename></member>
      <member><filename>/usr/lib/systemd/timestampd.conf</filename></member>
      <member><filename>/etc/systemd/timestampd.conf.d/*.conf</filename></member>
      <member><filename>/run/systemd/timestampd.conf.d/*.conf</filename></member>
      <member><filename>/usr/local/lib/systemd/timestampd.conf.d/*.conf</filename></member>
      <member><filename>/usr/lib/systemd/timestampd.conf.d/*.conf</filename></member>
    </simplelist></para>
  </refsynopsisdiv>

  <refsect1>
    <title>Description</title>

    <para>This file configures the Time-Stamp Authority contacted by
    <citerefentry><refentrytitle>systemd-timestampd.service</refentrytitle><manvolnum>8</manvolnum></citerefentry>.
    See <citerefentry><refentrytitle>systemd.syntax</refentrytitle><manvolnum>7</manvolnum></citerefentry>
    for a general description of the syntax.</para>
  </refsect1>

  <xi:include href="standard-conf.xml" xpointer="main-conf" />

  <refsect1>
    <title>Options</title>

    <para>The following options are available in the <literal>[Timestamp]</literal> section:</para>

    <variablelist class='config-directives'>

      <varlistentry>
        <term><varname>Authority=</varname></term>

        <listitem><para>The default Time-Stamp Authority to contact. Must be a URL with an
        <literal>http://</literal>, <literal>https://</literal> or <literal>tcp://</literal> scheme; the
        scheme selects the RFC 3161 transport to use. For the <literal>tcp://</literal> scheme a port may be
        specified (<literal>tcp://host:port</literal>); if omitted, port 318 is used. A Varlink caller may
        override this per request. If unset and no authority is supplied by the caller, requests will fail.</para>

        <xi:include href="version-info.xml" xpointer="v262"/></listitem>
      </varlistentry>

      <varlistentry>
        <term><varname>DataSizeMax=</varname></term>

        <listitem><para>The maximum amount of data that will be digested on behalf of a client that passes
        a file descriptor rather than a precomputed digest. Defaults to 1G. Takes a size in bytes, optionally
        suffixed with the usual K, M, G and T units (to the base of 1024), or
        <literal>infinity</literal> to impose no limit. Digesting happens synchronously, so this bounds how
        long a single client can keep the service from answering other clients.</para>

        <xi:include href="version-info.xml" xpointer="v262"/></listitem>
      </varlistentry>

      <varlistentry>
        <term><varname>ConnectionTimeoutSec=</varname></term>

        <listitem><para>The maximum time to wait for the authority to respond to a request. Defaults to
        90 seconds. Takes a value in seconds or one of the other time units understood by
        <citerefentry><refentrytitle>systemd.time</refentrytitle><manvolnum>7</manvolnum></citerefentry>.</para>

        <xi:include href="version-info.xml" xpointer="v262"/></listitem>
      </varlistentry>

    </variablelist>
  </refsect1>

